    "title": "Historically large crowd honors Seahawks on signing day - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Karli Koskovich ,\n45 minutes ago\nSANTA ROSA BEACH, Fla. (WMBB) – Ten South Walton High School athletes signed letters of intent on Wednesday, November 12.\nThe class includes one soccer player, one softball standout, two pole vaulters and six baseball players.\nSouth Walton principal Nina Borthwick and the Seahawks athletic staff honored the group in front of what was described as the biggest crowd the event has ever seen.\nSoccer player, Bailey Masche signed to play soccer at Ouachita Baptist University.\nTatum Kreinus signed to play softball at the University of Alabama at Birmingham.\nBrothers Beck and Pierce Williams will both compete in pole vault at the University of South Alabama.\nHead baseball coach Nick Borthwick celebrated six of his players taking the next step.\nGriffin Loy will play at Virginia. Nathan Whitney will play at Gulf Coast State College. Hudson Quinn will play at Wallace Community College. Jace Cunningham will play at Wallace Community College. Parker Granse will play at Auburn University. Coleman Borthwick will play at Auburn University “We’ve gotten to where we’re at because of their commitment to baseball and putting in the time,” Coach Borthwick said. “Every one of them has grown up loving baseball, the training, the travel, the work. It’s so special to see it pay off.”\nFor Borthwick, this year carried extra meaning as his son, Coleman, officially signed to play in the S.E.C. for the Auburn Tigers.\n“Whenever I first went to Auburn for a camp in seventh grade, I knew immediately, the campus, the people those were my people,” Coleman said.\n“When they offered me, it was life-changing. I’ve been waiting for this moment my whole life, and I can’t wait to step foot on campus and make my family and everyone who supported me proud.”\nSouth Walton’s latest signing class marks another milestone for the high school, holding a strong history of sending athletes to collegiate athletics.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to mypanhandle.com.",
